          "text": "Clinical Indication:  \nHistory of focal seizures with impaired awareness, beginning at age 25, occurring approximately twice per year. The reported etiology is immune-mediated, associated with an LGI1 antibody. Seizures are reported to be drug responsive. Current antiseizure medication: carbamazepine.\n\nTechnique:  \nRoutine scalp EEG recording was obtained using standard electrode placement and standard recording procedures.\n\nFindings:  \nThe available clinical information does not specify the waking or sleep background, focal slowing, interictal epileptiform discharges, or electrographic seizures. These EEG features cannot be characterized from the supplied data.\n\nImpression:  \nClinical history of focal seizures with impaired awareness, with onset at age 25 and frequency of approximately two episodes per year. Reported immune-mediated etiology with LGI1 antibody. Seizures are drug responsive on current carbamazepine therapy. No specific electrographic interpretation can be provided from the available EEG information.",
